sections.construction and validation of a lactyla:
The construction of a lactylation-m6A-informed prognostic signature involved genes significantly associated with survival ( P < 0.01) into a LASSO Cox regression model, facilitated by the “glmnet” R package. We employed ten-fold cross-validation to determine the optimal penalty coefficient (λ). The specific process was as follows: the dataset was randomly divided into 10 subsets, and each subset was used as the training set for 9 times while the remaining 1 time was used as the validation set. This process was repeated 10 times. By minimizing the mean of the cross-validation errors, we selected the optimal λ value within a standard error to ensure the simplicity and robustness of the model. The TCGA dataset was designated as the training dataset. The risk score calculation followed the equation: \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
